.TH TINYDNS-EDIT 1 "2026-07-23" "rgbdns 0.6.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tinydns-edit \- add a record to tinydns source data
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tinydns-edit
.I data data.new add mode domain address
.SH DESCRIPTION
Adds a record using a temporary file and replaces the data file on success.
.I mode
is one of ns, childns, host, alias, mx, host6, or alias6. IPv6 addresses are
accepted for host6 and alias6; other modes require IPv4.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tinydns-data (1)
